// The section "Conditions and loops" of the English guide; guide.rk lists the sections.

import { Example } from "../../example.rk"

export comp Control() {
    return <>
        <p>
            Conditions and loops are as in Go: no parentheses around the condition and always braces.
            There is one loop, <code>for</code>: over an array, with a condition, and the classic one
            with three parts. It also goes over a <code>Map</code>, by keys and values, over a
            {" "}<code>Set</code> and a typed array, which is indexed as an array is.
            {" "}<code>switch</code> has no <code>break</code>: each case ends by itself.
        </p>
        <Example name="control" />
        <p>
            As in Go, <code>if</code> and <code>switch</code> can start with an initializer:
            {" "}<code>if const n, err = parse(text); err != null</code>. Its variables are seen in
            every branch and not after the statement. A label before a loop lets <code>break</code>
            {" "}and <code>continue</code> in a nested loop leave the outer one.
        </p>
        <Example name="labels" />
    </>
}
